# Range access syntax has been removed. This test now exercises key-not-found
# via dot access on a dict with only Int and String keys.
# The dict has mixed key types; accessing a missing key produces an error.
[data: [a: 1  b: 2]]

data.missing
=== error
[E001] key not found: missing (available keys: a, b)

=== warn
field 'missing' not found in [a: 1 b: 2] at 5:1-5:13
